# Frontend: Vite and React 19

`{{ fp }}src/`: the app (`App.tsx`, entry `main.tsx`), its components, its API client
(`lib/`), its constants (`constants.ts`); `{{ fp }}index.html` is the page Vite serves. Read
`{{ fp }}AGENTS.md` first. Run: `kiln dev`; check: `kiln check` (ESLint, `tsc`); tests:
`pnpm test` (Vitest).

## Code

- **[STRICT-TS]** Strict TypeScript in every `.ts` and `.tsx` (`strict`,
  `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`, `exactOptionalPropertyTypes`).
- **[NO-ANY]** No `any`: `unknown`, then a type narrowing (ESLint rule).
- **[ASYNC-AWAIT]** `async/await` with `try/catch` only; `.then().catch()` chains are banned.
- **[MODERN-REACT]** React 19: function components and hooks, never a class component. The
  rules of hooks hold (ESLint, `react-hooks`). Asynchronous data is read with `use()` and
  `Suspense`, or an effect that ignores an answer arriving after the component is gone.
- **[API-CALLS]** Components never call the API directly: they go through a typed function of
  `src/lib/` that validates the response before returning it.
- **[UI-STATES]** Every screen that loads data handles the three states explicitly: loading,
  error (an understandable message) and empty list.
- **[ACCESSIBILITY]** Every field has an associated `<label>`, every icon button an `aria-label`,
  every informative image an `alt`. Everything works with the keyboard and focus stays visible.
- **[TEST-DENSITY]** The front's test density never drops: its floor in `charter.toml` is raised
  as it goes up (floor). A component is tested through what it renders (Vitest).

## Styling

- **[STYLE-2]** **Tailwind by default**, right in the markup. Separate CSS only for a multi-step
  animation, a native browser element or a black-box third-party component.
- **[STYLE-3]** `src/index.css` is the only CSS file, imported by `main.tsx`: it imports Tailwind
  and holds the theme tokens (`@theme`). A component writes the class of a token, never an
  arbitrary value that copies it.
- **[STYLE-5]** Banned: bursts of arbitrary classes, `@apply` to rebuild a component,
  `!important` except to override a third-party library that forces it.
{%- if level >= 2 %}

## Performance and quality

- **[CORE-WEB-VITALS]** Budgets at the 75th percentile, on mobile: **LCP < 2.5 s**,
  **INP < 200 ms**, **CLS < 0.1**. A regression beyond them blocks the release.
- **[JS-BUDGET]** A JavaScript budget for the bundle, checked at build time; a route that is
  not on the first screen is loaded lazily (`lazy()`).
- **[AUTOMATED-ACCESSIBILITY]** Main pages pass an automated `axe-core` check; target
  **WCAG 2.2 level AA**.
{%- endif %}
